        <mxCell id="9l-V8SlR0vPhBhPmiidy-130" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;Prompt Caching&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=30;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-270" y="30" width="700" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9l-V8SlR0vPhBhPmiidy-134" value="&lt;div style=&quot;display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; text-align: left; align-items: baseline; font-size: 0; line-height: 1.25;margin-top: -2px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Prompt caching&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt; is a performance optimization technique used by AI platforms (like OpenAI’s API) to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;store and reuse the results of previous prompts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt; instead of recomputing them every time. &#xa;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; text-align: left; align-items: baseline; font-size: 0; line-height: 1.25;margin-top: -2px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;In simple terms: &#xa;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding-left: 10px;list-style-position: inside; list-style-type:disc&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align:left;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left: 0px;margin-top: -2px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;When you send a prompt (e.g., a long system message or a large context) that doesn’t change often, the model can&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;that part.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align:left;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left: 0px;margin-top: -2px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;On later requests, if the cached prompt or its prefix is reused, the model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;skips re-processing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;it, saving&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;latency and cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:23.3px;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="html=1;overflow=block;blockSpacing=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;spacing=3.8;strokeColor=none;fillOpacity=0;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=0;lucidId=z1oZlhC9rRzN;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-210" y="130" width="550" height="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;span data-lucid-type=&quot;application/vnd.lucid.text&quot; data-lucid-content=&quot;{&amp;quot;t&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Each vendor has its own prompt caching mechanism. By understanding the mechanism, we can greatly lower the cost.&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;m&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;a&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:40,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:112},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;fc&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Regular&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:112},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;fid&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:947029,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:112}]}&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:30px;&quot;&gt;Each vendor has its own prompt caching mechanism. By understanding the mechanism, we can greatly lower the cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" id="9l-V8SlR0vPhBhPmiidy-135">
          <mxCell style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry x="-220" y="500" width="560" height="170" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
